commit ad631ed46786e21c6602239cb55528aa65c6a2f6
Author: Jan Ziak <0xe2.0x9a.0x9b@xfce.org>
Date:   Sun Mar 21 06:53:06 2021 +0100

    Add a simple network bandwidth monitor (uses libgtop as a fallback)
    
    The implementation uses /proc/net/netstat by default (if it is available)
    because it is more efficient than using libgtop. It takes about 250
    syscalls for libgtop to obtain information about a couple of network
    interfaces, while it takes just a few syscalls to read /proc/net/netstat.
    
    A full network bar (100% network load) corresponds to a constant of
    100 Mbit/s. Bandwidths higher than 100 Mbit/s are clamped to 100%.
    The tooltip however is showing non-clamped bandwidth rounded to Mbit/s.
    
    Closes: https://gitlab.xfce.org/panel-plugins/xfce4-systemload-plugin/-/issues/14

